[2026-06-19T20:19:57.138Z] [INFO] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_111","type":"reasoning","text":"**Managing Git commits**\n\nI need to commit, but first, I’ve got to handle the untracked ci-logs. I should only add the necessary files before the commit. If the logs are to be preserved, I can add `ci-logs/` to .git/info/exclude. I’m wondering if I can use apply_patch to edit that exclusion file. It seems safe since it typically doesn't interfere with commits. I’ll check if it contains what I need with grep, then apply the patch to ensure those logs are ignored. No need to commit right away!"}}
